Gate 0 closure — changes to the recovered prototype

Applied automatically by scripts/gate0/run_prototype_suite.py, which will not
run the suite unless these are present. Manual equivalent, from the prototype
root:

    git apply -p1 gate0-closure.patch

The frozen archive at %LOCALAPPDATA%\TitlePipe\gate0-prototype-archive stays
as-recovered and hash-verified against GATE_0_ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.md. This is the
delta, in VCS so the closure is not machine-local.

Four changes:

  seed.py       _docx_text falls back to python-docx when pandoc is absent.
                pandoc was the only reader, so a missing system binary made two
                orders silently vanish from the seed — indistinguishable from a
                missing report.

  assemble.py   build_report retains the pre-suppression sets for BOTH
                mortgages and lien-bearing documents. Without them a lien
                suppressed for a permitted reason and one dropped by chain
                termination are indistinguishable — the distinction R15 turns
                on.

  validators.py v14_liens_survive_chain_termination, the assertion R15 mandated
                and Gate 0 found missing. Covers mortgages, judgments, liens and
                UCC filings; identifies instruments by recording identity rather
                than object identity; allowlists permitted suppression reasons
                and explicitly refuses chain-based ones. In HARD_VALIDATORS.
                Fails closed when either pre-suppression set is absent.

  test_seed.py  TITLEPIPE_SEED_ROOT makes the delivered-report root
                configurable. It defaulted to /mnt/user-data, a path in the
                sandbox the prototype was written in.

Contains no client-derived party names, addresses or amounts.

